Package: SHpamm
Title: Subdistribution Hazard Piecewise Exponential Additive Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Juan Carlos", "Espinosa-Moreno", role = "aut"),
    person("Fernando", "García-García", role = "aut"),
    person("Andreas", "Bender", role = "aut"),
    person("Dae-Jin", "Lee", email = "dae-jin.lee@ie.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description: Fits flexible subdistribution hazard models for competing risks
    using weighted piecewise exponential additive models. Implements exact
    interval-averaged censoring weights, smooth effects through 'mgcv',
    cumulative incidence prediction, and subject-level and stacked sandwich
    variance approximations. The fixed-dimensional variance theory does not
    guarantee coverage for penalised smooth functions.
